  "job_B3.3.11_20251003_114653": {
    "text": "Of Jacobe, Johannes Bro\u00f0er.\n\u00d0\u00e6t Judeissce folc brohte \u00fean hundredes ealdren feo, for \u00fey \u00fe\u00e6t heo mosten Jacoben swa ateon swa heo\nHeo genamen hine \u00fea & hine geh\u00e6ften.\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 mycel geflit betwux \u00fean cristenan & \u00fean h\u00e6\u00f0enan.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 sum \u00fe\u00e6t hit riht w\u00e6re \u00fe\u00e6t man l\u00e6dde Jacoben for\u00f0 to heora gesamnunge, & geherdan his word\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don \u00fea sunderhalgen to Jacobe, Hwy bodest \u00feu \u00feone H\u00e6lend, \u00fee w\u00e6s ahangen, swa swa we ealle\nJacobus so\u00f0lice w\u00e6s afylled mid \u00fean Halgen Gaste, & heom to cw\u00e6\u00f0, Gehyre\u00f0 nu bro\u00f0re \u00fea leofeste,\nUre Drihten behet Abrahame ure f\u00e6der \u00fe\u00e6t on his s\u00e6de by\u00f0 yrfeweardod ealle \u00feeoden.\nSo\u00f0lice his s\u00e6d n\u00e6s na ofer Ismaele, ac ofer Isaac, swa swa God sylf cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Abrahame, On Isaac by\u00f0\n& so\u00f0lice ure f\u00e6der Abraham w\u00e6s geteald to Godes freond \u00e6r \u00fean \u00fee he embsny\u00f0en w\u00e6re, & \u00e6r \u00fean\nGyf \u00feonne Abraham is geworden Godes freond gelyfende, hwy mycele swy\u00f0ere by\u00f0 se Godes feond \u00fee\n\u00dea Judees cw\u00e6don, Hw\u00e6t is se \u00fee ne gelef\u00f0 on God?\nJacobus andswerode, Se \u00fee ne gelef\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t on Abrahames cynne by\u00f0 geerfeweard ealle \u00feeode, & se \u00fee\n\u00deiss he forewitegode \u00feurh God sylfne & \u00feurh his wissunge.\nEft Isaias forewytegode beo ures Drihtenes tocyme & cw\u00e6\u00f0, Efne m\u00e6den by\u00f0 geeacnod on inno\u00f0e, &\nEft Jeremias cw\u00e6\u00f0, Eala \u00feu Jerusalem, efne \u00fein alesend cum\u00f0 & \u00feiss by\u00f0 his tacne.\nBlinde eagen he onlihte\u00f0, & deafen he forgyf\u00f0 gehyrnysse, & mid his stefne he awec\u00f0 deade to life.\nEft Ezechiel se wytega cwy\u00f0\u00f0, Eala \u00feu Syon, \u00fein king cum\u00f0 & \u00fee gesta\u00f0ele\u00f0.\nDaniel so\u00f0lice cw\u00e6\u00f0, Swa swa mannes bearn God cum\u00f0 to mannen, & he geahne\u00f0 him ealdordomes &\n& so\u00f0lice se Halga Gast clypode \u00feurh Dauid & \u00feuss cw\u00e6\u00f0, Min Drihten cw\u00e6\u00f0 to mine Drihtene, \u00feu\nEft f\u00e6der st\u00e6fne w\u00e6s gehyrd of heofone \u00feuss cwe\u00f0ende, He geceg\u00f0 me his f\u00e6der & ic hine asette ofer\nTo Dauiden sylfen God cw\u00e6\u00f0, Of w\u00e6stme \u00feines inno\u00f0es ic sette ofer \u00feinne hehsetle.\nBeo his \u00ferowunge so\u00f0lice Isaias se witega cw\u00e6\u00f0, Swa swa unsca\u00f0ig lamb God w\u00e6s gel\u00e6dd to slege.\nEft Dauid cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00feurh \u00feone Halgen Gast, Heo adrifen mine handen & mine fet & gerimdan ealle mine\nHeo so\u00f0lice me ymbsceawodan & me beheoldan & tod\u00e6ldan min reaf & hluten heom betwynen.\nEft on o\u00f0re stowe se witega cw\u00e6\u00f0 beo ures Drihtenes \u00ferowunge, Heo s\u00e6nden on minne mete gealle &\nBeo his dea\u00f0e so\u00f0lice is gecwe\u00f0en, Min fl\u00e6sc reste\u00f0 on hyhte, for \u00fean \u00fee \u00feu ne forl\u00e6test mine sawle on\nEft beo his \u00e6riste he sylf cw\u00e6\u00f0 to his F\u00e6der, Ic arise of dea\u00f0e & ic cume to \u00fee & mid \u00fee wunige, & for\nBeo his upastigennysse is awriten so\u00f0lice \u00fe\u00e6t, He asteah on hehnysse & \u00fea geh\u00e6fte he gel\u00e6dde of\nEft Anna, Samueles moder, cw\u00e6\u00f0, Drihten asteah geond heofones & his mihte ateowde, & manege\n& he nu sitt \u00e6t his F\u00e6der swy\u00f0re, & cum\u00f0 to demen cwican & deaden swa swa se witega cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ure\n\u00deas \u00feing synden sume gefyllode eornestlice on uren Drihtene H\u00e6lende Criste & for\u00f0gewitene, & \u00fea \u00fea\nSo\u00f0lice Isaias cw\u00e6\u00f0 beo \u00fean mycelen dome \u00fee toweard is, \u00fe\u00e6t deade arise\u00f0 of heora byrigene, & by\u00f0\nEac Dauid se salmscop cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t God h\u00e6f\u00f0 \u00feone mihte \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00e6ighwylcen m\u00e6nn forgelt beo his\nNu bidde ic leofa gebro\u00f0re, cw\u00e6\u00f0 Sanctus Jacobus, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6ighwylc eower d\u00e6dbote do his synnen, \u00fe\u00e6t he\nSe \u00fee hine sylfne wat beo \u00e6nige d\u00e6le scyldigne, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00fe\u00e6s \u00ferowunge geyfelode \u00fee ealne middeneard\nFor \u00fean witodlice ne by\u00f0 nane m\u00e6nn d\u00e6dbote alefd \u00e6fter \u00feyssen life, ac h\u00e6f\u00f0 \u00e6ighwylc an swa swa he\nEornestlice Dauid cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00feurh \u00feone Halgen Gast beo Drihtene, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea Judees agulden him yfel for gode,\nWitodlice he ar\u00e6rde creoperes of heora cynne, \u00fee alefede w\u00e6ron, & hreoflen he gecl\u00e6nsode, blinde he\n& eac \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6s forewitegod \u00feurh Dauid hwu his agen discipul hine bel\u00e6wde & to dea\u00f0e gesealde, \u00fea he\nEalle \u00feas \u00feing, leofe gebro\u00f0re, Abrahames bearn fores\u00e6dan \u00feurh \u00feone halgen Gast.\nHw\u00e6t wene \u00fee nu gyf ge gelyfen nylle\u00f0 on God, \u00fe\u00e6t ge mugen \u00e6twinden \u00fean ecen wite \u00feonne o\u00f0re\nIc cwe\u00f0e, \u00fe\u00e6t ge wel wur\u00f0e syn \u00fe\u00e6t ge gewitnode beon.\nAc ge age\u00f0 mycele \u00feearfe, \u00fe\u00e6t ge d\u00e6dbote don eower synnen mid teare gyten, & mid heofunge,\n& heo mid lege forb\u00e6rnde wurdon.\n\u00deas \u00feing & o\u00f0re gelice, Jacobus bodede \u00fean folca swa lange, \u00fe\u00e6t God \u00e6lmihtig him gety\u00f0ede swa\nWe bidde\u00f0 eadmodlice nu, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu t\u00e6ce us d\u00e6dbote to done.\nSanctus Jacobus heom andswerede, Eale ge leofe gebro\u00f0re, ne scule ge nateshwan eow for\u00f0\u00e6ncen.\nGelyfe\u00f0 on God & by\u00f0 gefulhtnede, \u00feonne by\u00f0 ealle eower synnen adilogode.\n\u00c6fter feawe dagen so\u00f0lice Abiathar se h\u00e6\u00f0ene biscop geseh \u00fe\u00e6t swa mycel menige \u00fe\u00e6s folcas on\n\u00dea astyrede he mycele saca on \u00fean folca, & swy\u00f0lice ceaste \u00feurh his feoh gestreon, swa \u00fe\u00e6t an of \u00fean\nSe w\u00e6s Archelaus sune.\nHe het \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6t me hine beheafdigen scolde, & \u00fea \u00fea me hine to beheafdunge l\u00e6dde.\n\u00dea geseh he sumne creopere licgende on his weige & \u00feuss him to clypigende w\u00e6s, S\u00e6inte Jacob\nSe halge Jacobus him andswerode, On mines Drihtenes name H\u00e6lendes Cristes, \u00fee onhangen w\u00e6s on\nHe \u00fe\u00e6rrihte aras, & ongann blissigende eornen.\n& bletsigen Drihtenes name H\u00e6lendes Cristes.\n\u00dea se sunderhalge Josias \u00fe\u00e6t geseh, \u00fee hine \u00e6r to beheafdunge gel\u00e6dde, ongann feallen to Jacobes\n\u00dea undergeat se halge Jacobus \u00fe\u00e6t his heorte w\u00e6s geneosod fram \u00fean \u00e6lmihtigan Gode, & cw\u00e6\u00f0 to\nJosias andswerode, Ic gelefe, & \u00fe\u00e6t is min geleafe nu o\u00f0\u00f0 \u00feysne time \u00fe\u00e6t he is \u00fe\u00e6s lyfigendan Godes\n\u00dea w\u00e6s eall \u00feiss gecy\u00f0d \u00fean ealdorbiscope, \u00fee Abiathar hatte, & he let \u00fea geh\u00e6ften Josiam & him to\nJosias andswerode, Aweregod beo \u00feu & ealle \u00feine lease godes, for \u00fean \u00fee \u00feu awendest \u00fee fram \u00fe\u00e6s\nMines Drihtenes name, so\u00f0lice H\u00e6lendes Cristes \u00fee Jacobus bode\u00f0, is gebletsod on ecnysse.\n\u00dea het Abiathar beaten his mu\u00f0 \u00feearle swy\u00f0e, & hine sy\u00f0\u00f0en s\u00e6nde to Heroden, & gewrit mid him\n\u00dea heo becomen so\u00f0lice to \u00fe\u00e6re stowe \u00fe\u00e6r me hine beheafdigen scolde, \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Sanctus Jacobus to\nSe halge Jacobus cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Josiam, Gelyfst \u00feu on ures Drihtenes namen H\u00e6lendes Cristes \u00fe\u00e6s\nHe andswerode, Ic gelefe.\nSe halge Jacobus hine begeat \u00fea mid \u00fean w\u00e6tere & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0, Forgyf me sibbne coss.\nMid \u00fean \u00fee Josias hine cyssinde w\u00e6s, \u00fea as\u00e6nde he his hand ofer his heafod & worhte Cristes\nJosias wear\u00f0 \u00fea fullfremod on geleafen ures Drihtenes H\u00e6lendes Cristes & on \u00e6nne time samod mid\n\u00dean sy wuldor & wur\u00f0mynt a on ealra wurlde wurld, Amen.",
